From: Plain Browser
Subject: [ui] Browser windows in the MSIX package: the package's taskbar icon, not the profile icon

Category: 60-ui. Installed from the Microsoft Store, the browser runs from an MSIX package. Its writes to
%LOCALAPPDATA%\PlainBrowser go to the package's virtualized copy (Packages\<family>\LocalCache\Local) unless that
folder already exists for real, which on a machine that never ran the portable build it does not. Chromium gives
each browser window relaunch details whose icon is the profile's "Google Profile.ico" at the real path; Explorer
(outside the package) does not see the virtualized file, so the taskbar button was a blank page.
When the process belongs to a package, a browser window now gets only the package app's App User Model ID
(<PackageFamilyName>!PlainBrowser) and no relaunch details: the taskbar groups it with the Start entry and shows the
package's logo (branding/icons/msix). Web app windows (earlier return) and the portable build are unchanged.
---
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_property_manager_win.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_property_manager_win.cc
@@ -5,5 +5,9 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_window_property_manager_win.h"
 
+#include <windows.h>
+
+#include <appmodel.h>
+
 #include "base/command_line.h"
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
 #include "base/strings/utf_string_conversions.h"
@@ -26,4 +30,19 @@
 
 using extensions::ExtensionRegistry;
 
+namespace {
+
+// Plain Browser: the App User Model ID of the MSIX package's app
+// (<PackageFamilyName>!PlainBrowser) when the browser runs from the package
+// (Microsoft Store), empty otherwise.
+std::wstring PackageAppUserModelId() {
+  wchar_t id[APPLICATION_USER_MODEL_ID_MAX_LENGTH];
+  UINT32 length = APPLICATION_USER_MODEL_ID_MAX_LENGTH;
+  return ::GetCurrentApplicationUserModelId(&length, id) == ERROR_SUCCESS
+             ? std::wstring(id)
+             : std::wstring();
+}
+
+}  // namespace
+
 BrowserWindowPropertyManager::BrowserWindowPropertyManager(
@@ -87,4 +106,14 @@
   }
 
+  // Plain Browser: inside the MSIX package the window takes the package app's
+  // ID and no relaunch details. The profile icon they point to is written to
+  // the package's virtualized AppData, which Explorer does not see, so the
+  // taskbar showed a blank page; the package's logo is used instead.
+  if (std::wstring package_app_id = PackageAppUserModelId();
+      !package_app_id.empty()) {
+    ui::win::SetAppIdForWindow(package_app_id, hwnd_);
+    return;
+  }
